      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.08,
          "en": "Instructor: Would be nice to be more specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.08,
          "end": 6.3,
          "en": "about that error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.3,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "Now if you inspect the response we're getting back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 11.73,
          "en": "you can, of course, see that on the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.73,
          "end": 13.98,
          "en": "we have that error field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 16.71,
          "en": "And if we dig into that, there's another error field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.71,
          "end": 18.84,
          "en": "so a nested error.error field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 21.69,
          "en": "And if we dig into that, we see we have a message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "That's a message provided by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "And if you have a look at the Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 29.34,
          "en": "REST API documentation, and you scroll down a bit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 32.85,
          "en": "you see common error codes that are thrown by that endpoint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.85,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "And that would be, for example, EMAIL_EXISTS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 38.4,
          "en": "So, in the end, we just have to check for these codes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.4,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "and we can output a more helpful error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 46.71,
          "en": "Now we could do that here in our component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 48.06,
          "en": "Here, where we get that error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "we could check with a switch statement, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "If my error response, maybe we should name this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 58.65,
          "en": "errorRes to be more specific about what this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.65,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "because it's the full response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 64.41,
          "en": "And on there, we have a error key, and we have an error key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.41,
          "end": 66.03,
          "en": "and there, we have a message key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.03,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "We switch on that message, and then we have a case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 72.42,
          "en": "where this is EMAIL_EXISTS, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 77.42,
          "en": "And now we set this error to 'This email exists already',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.84,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "for example, like this, instead of doing it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "If we would save that code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.39,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "it already should do its job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "And if I try signing up with that email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 91.28999999999999,
          "en": "I get the email exists already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.28999999999999,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "Now we could do that here by handling everything off",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "that here in the component is not necessarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 99.87,
          "en": "the best possible way of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 102.75,
          "en": "It moves too much logic into the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.75,
          "end": 106.02000000000001,
          "en": "which should primarily focus on updating the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 109.02000000000001,
          "en": "and not so much about handling the response correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.02000000000001,
          "end": 111.45,
          "en": "And that, therefore, screams for the usage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.45,
          "end": 115.83,
          "en": "of an RxJS operator that allows us to handle errors here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.83,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "in the service in our observable chain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 120.963,
          "en": "we're setting up here, so on this observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.92,
          "end": 125.19,
          "en": "For that, we can simply pipe on this observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.19,
          "end": 127.38,
          "en": "and add RxJS operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.38,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "And here I am interested in one operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 133.65,
          "en": "and that is the catchError operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 138.65,
          "en": "Now catchError needs to be imported from rxjs/operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 141.36,
          "en": "to be available in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.36,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "And we will also need one other thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 149.48,
          "en": "and that will be the throwError function from just 'rxjs',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "which will create a new observable that wraps an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "Because if you remember the earlier sections in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.26,
          "end": 160.53,
          "en": "RxJS always needs to return an observable down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.53,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "and catchError catches the error, but you still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "then need to return a new observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 167.76,
          "en": "and that observable should still wrap the error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.76,
          "end": 169.77,
          "en": "so that it still ends up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 171.9,
          "en": "in that error case, in our subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.9,
          "end": 173.46,
          "en": "And we do want to end up there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.46,
          "end": 175.71,
          "en": "I just want to move more logic from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.71,
          "end": 177.57,
          "en": "into the observable chain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.57,
          "end": 181.02,
          "en": "And indeed, therefore, we can grab that switch statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.02,
          "end": 183.12,
          "en": "and move it into here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.12,
          "end": 186.15,
